{"body":{"text":["The chassis's look holds its tokens, which every component draws with and a site tunes, and what the chassis makes itself, a drawing's host, a note and its inspector, in `chassis/web/look/`. A link is made in one place, `chassis/web/href.ts`, as the page keeps its address, and no component reads the address: an answer says what was asked by its steps, as the pills say them, and a list keeps how it was shown by what it holds. The breadcrumb is one read of `wholes` and the start one of `roots`, functions written in the language. The components hand the chassis what it needs in one call, and the chassis gives a component no answer the same as the last. A component picked for a use is written strictly, from the heads its use was read at. *The session's, at the author's word to clean what it could before he reviews (20/21); built.*"]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a use naming no component gives is drawn by the component that takes it, found by `taking`, a function of the language, not the chassis's: of the functions or components it is given to choose among, those that take all that is given, as a use giving it would be judged, some placeholder taking something given of a type of the field it takes. So a brief draws as a brief, and a list with the direction it runs as a list. Whether a function or a component takes what is given is the native `takes`, giving what each placeholder takes, or null: native because how a use's args meet an input is the evaluator's own, so the rule is written once and the chassis rebuilds nothing of the engine. The author asked for finding as one simple expression: \"It should just be one simple expression, right?\" (20/25), matching every argument: \"we match against multiple arguments, not only one\" (20/27). A component over a kind of value alone, a list or a string, is never found so, since many take one shape for different ends, and is drawn only where a use names it; what nothing takes by a type is drawn by the fallback the chassis is given, Value, showing any holon as its values, so nothing is left unshown, and what holds no holon is given it at once, nothing read. One found is written into the use as its `fn` where the use's store takes the change, and found again each time where not; where several fit, a chooser lists them and the person's pick is drawn, never guessed. *Picked once and written, proposed, 18/88; finding as one expression over every argument, the author's (20/25, 20/27); takes and taking the session's (20/28); the name `taking` the session's, taken by the author (20/32, 20/33); built.*"]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading Knowledge as text takes about a quarter of a second at the command line over the five stores, where it took 0.8 s while every word was a holon (19/49). A brief is read in one read, by `sections`, a function written in the language upon the natives: a brief and the briefs it holds as sections, each a whole entering no brief, which the brief component applies, where it read a whole for every brief, level by level (20/16). A read learns what it applies before working it out, a layer at a time from the expression it carries, each layer one question of every store, and a function it names asked whole, the function and all it holds, its input and its body however deep, in one question, so it learns in a round for each function named and never one for each use within one, the next layer read off what a whole gave while the other stores are asked of it alongside (20/34); and a kind of value is told by its type alone, a kind's name and an empty mould, so it is never searched for (20/14, 20/16). Counted in rounds one after another, finding a component for a brief takes about 6 where it took 20, the breadcrumb's `wholes` 9 where 23, `sections` of The design 13 where 18, and a brief's `whole` about 6 (20/34); what a read applies is still learned every read; in the browser, once the field is fetched, a move to a brief settled in 60 to 116 ms where it took 155 to 1,269 once a brief was read in one read (20/16), and measures 86 to 129 ms since, the rounds no longer what sets it (20/34). The engine's whole asking each store its whole as one question was built again and measured: beside the brief's one read it came within about 10 ms of the layered whole, so it stays let go (19/73, 20/14). The engine still lets go of what a use gives beyond what its function takes, without a word, which is to be refused, since nothing is to fail silently (19/39). Still between: `language/text.ts` keeps the earlier form of expressions for its own tests alone. *The read's shape the session's, at the author's word that things be as simple as possible (20/15); built.*"]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ003","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ004","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ005","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Reading git from a browser, tested:** a repository served as plain files read from a page, with no proxy and no limit, before building on it (19/24)."]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ006","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
