{"body":{"text":["Natives are small pure functions in code, in families: the lazy ones, `if`, `case`, `and`, `or`; values; lists; sets, which are hashed; holons, `holon`, `whole`, `in`, `out`, `follow`, `takes`; history, `log`; and patterns; and the pairs glass ships, `parse` and `print`, `steps` and `chain`, with `each`, `group` and the way back, `back`. Beside them stand legacy natives, `type`, `store`, `named`, `children` and `since` among them, kept only while functions written in the field still call them. Everything else is written in the field upon the natives, as `sections`, which the brief component reads by, `wholes` and `roots`, and `taking`, by which the chassis finds a component (20/16, 20/22, 20/28, 20/34)."]},"id":"1M84FFHN9BNZ00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}